1
00:00:03,401 --> 00:00:07,398
Re-measure before cutting: the Ortiz back wall is 119", not 121".

2
00:00:07,398 --> 00:00:12,271
Record the revision in the job notes first.

3
00:00:12,271 --> 00:00:24,839
On the Room tab, type the new width.

4
00:00:24,839 --> 00:00:29,488
The app flags it straight away: the 3-5/16" filler F1 now runs past the wall.

5
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:33,512
The filler was cut to the old gap. The warning offers the fix: shrink F1 to the new gap.

6
00:00:33,512 --> 00:00:38,469
F1 keeps its edge against the run and is cut back at the wall, to 1-5/16".

7
00:00:38,469 --> 00:00:42,733
The warning is gone: the run meets the 119" wall again. Nothing else had to change.

8
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:47,980
Elevation of the back wall, with the narrower filler at the right end.

9
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:58,158
The cut list picks up the new filler size...

10
00:00:58,158 --> 00:01:03,875
...and nesting re-runs, so the labels and sheet maps match the revised job.

11
00:01:03,875 --> 00:01:08,078
A site change caught before cutting: one number in the room, one click on the filler, done.
